Subject: Goldfish games for 60-card decks (no commander)

The goldfish simulator only modelled Commander games: the deck's commander
starts in the command zone, opponents have 40 life and the first mulligan
is free. A decklist without a commander had its first line taken as the
commander, so a Standard or Modern deck was simulated as a 59-card deck
with one of its cards cast from the command zone. The gateway therefore
refused to simulate any deck without a commander.

goldfish_run, goldfish_ab and goldfish_annotate take `constructed` (default
false, so every existing call and run_id is unchanged). A constructed game:

- has no commander: every listed card is in the library, ' *CMDR*' markers
  are only stripped, and an Archidekt deck's premier category is not read;
- starts each opponent at 20 life (the kill is 20 damage);
- has no free first mulligan (London mulligan; mulligan.free_first still
  overrides);
- is on the play: no draw on turn 1.

The summary, the run header and the HTML report leave out the commander
lines and name the format instead. The run_id folds in "constructed" only
when it is set. Interactive games (goldfish_start) stay Commander-only.

Tests: tests/goldfish/test_constructed.py; the commander-note test in
tests/goldfish/test_server_tools.py follows _goldfish_load_deck's new
argument.

Upstream: Kautiontape/mystic-forge at dd82cd1 (main, 2026-10-04) simulates
Commander only. Drop this patch when upstream models 60-card games.

